    <string name="settings_about_entry">About &amp; guide</string>
    <string name="settings_about_entry_hint">What Kairos does, the priority score, the version</string>

    <string name="about_intro">Kairos ranks your tasks for the day and fits them into the gaps of your calendar, at the right time.</string>
    <string name="about_brief_title">In short</string>
    <string name="about_brief_1">It ranks the day’s tasks by a priority score, shown on each one.</string>
    <string name="about_brief_2">It fits each task into the gaps of the calendar, around meetings, with a buffer after each meeting.</string>
    <string name="about_brief_3">It protects deep-work blocks and lightens the afternoon slump.</string>
    <string name="about_brief_4">It tracks the time actually spent and compares it with the estimate.</string>
    <string name="about_score_title">The priority score (WSJF)</string>
    <string name="about_score_formula">score = (priority value + deadline urgency) ÷ effort</string>
    <string name="about_score_body">Value grows fourfold with each priority step (P0 is worth 4 times P1), the deadline weighs more and more as it approaches, and effort is measured in Fibonacci points. Small and important goes before big and distant. An overdue task always goes first.</string>
    <string name="about_name_title">Why “Kairos”?</string>
    <string name="about_name_body">In Greek, kairos means the opportune moment, the right instant to act, as opposed to chronos, time passing by. That is the tool’s job: finding the right slot for each task.</string>
